From fba3ea140a76f8a6a80a61658603859da0ed4ff7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:15:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] web: Explorar, the flare page driven by a time cursor (D-101)

Same hero, 4 AIA channels (image / difference), Grad-CAM and Centella
events vs GOES flares, over any period a Centella API (>= 2.2) holds: a
vendored-ECharts timeline with zoom, click-to-jump, playback and keyboard
steps; the instant lives in the URL hash. Data through whitelisted proxies
(explorar/datos/*.json, aia/<wave>.png?slot=, explorar/gradcam/<slot>.png)
to FLARE_ARCHIVE_URL (default: the live FLARE_NRT_URL), so a replayed
month can be browsed without touching the live page. Linked from the flare
page; disk marker uses the synoptic field of view. es/en.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019TiLZJK6V4V5hFsgBRSyAK
